{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ARTM95ZXuXVo7NbXZE7fk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tdescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t# BUILD & TEST\n6\t\n7\t## Commands\n8\t\n9\t```sh\n10\t# Tests (Babashka runner)\n11\tbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\n12\tbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\n13\tbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n14\t# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\n15\tbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\n16\tbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n17\tbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n18\tbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\n19\tbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n20\tbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n21\tbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\n22\tbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n23\tbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n24\t# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n25\t# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n26\t# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n27\t# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n28\t# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n29\t# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n30\t# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n31\t# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n32\t# Run one Dart lane at a time repo-wide.\n33\t#\n34\t# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n35\t# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n36\t# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n37\t# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n38\t# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n39\t# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n40\t# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n41\t# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n42\t# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n43\t# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n44\t# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n45\t# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n46\t# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n47\t# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n48\t# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n49\t# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n50\t# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n51\t# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time repo-wide to avoid contention.\n52\t# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n53\t# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n54\t# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n55\t# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\n56\tnpm test             # Node.js tests\n57\t\n58\t# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n59\t# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n60\t# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n61\t# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\n62\tbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\n63\tbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n64\t                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n65\t                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n66\t                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n70\t\n71\t`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\n72\treach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\n73\tmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\n74\ttests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\n75\tA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\n76\tfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\n77\tio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n78\t(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\n79\tlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\n80\tneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n81\t`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\n82\ttypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\n83\tland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\n84\tchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\n85\tantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\n86\tas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\n87\tdao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n88\t(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\n89\tand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n90\t\n91\t### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n92\t\n93\t`bb test:sub <subsystem>...` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the tests belonging to\n94\tone or more canonical subsystems (defined in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`). Selection\n95\tis by longest namespace prefix matching.\n96\t\n97\t```sh\n98\tbb test:sub <subsystem>...        # All three lanes in parallel (fast form)\n99\tbb test:sub:clj <subsystem>...    # JVM lane alone\n100\tbb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>...   # Node lane alone\n101\tbb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>...   # Dart lane alone\n102\tbb test:sub:list <subsystem>...   # Show namespaces, builds, Class B seams & dependents; runs nothing\n103\tbb test:sub <subsystem>... --slow # Include slow tests (-i :slow on JVM, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 on Node/Dart)\n104\tbb -cp src/dev -m affected-test   # Run affected-test self-tests directly in Babashka\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\t#### Canonical Subsystems (`src/dev/subsystems.edn`)\n108\t\n109\t- **Layer 0 (Core Data & Transport)**: `dao.stream`, `dao.jing`, `dao.data`, `dao.base`\n110\t- **Layer 1 (Space & UI)**: `dao.space`, `dao.gui`, `dao.postgraphics`\n111\t- **Layer 2 (Execution Engine)**: `yin.vm.ucf`, `yin.vm`\n112\t- **Layer 3 (Languages & Interop)**: `yin.repl`, `yang.python`, `yang.base`\n113\t- **Layer 4 (Applications & Demos)**: `demo`, `world`\n114\t- **Infrastructure**: `dev`, `bench`\n115\t\n116\tPrerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:python-antlr`)\n117\tand lane serialization (`[:clj :cljd]`) are derived purely from text reach of the\n118\tselected namespaces and run automatically when needed.\n119\t\n120\t#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n121\t\n122\t1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n123\t2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n124\t3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n125\t4. **G3 Master**: The mandatory landing gate on master after merge, and for any wide change (`bb test`).\n126\t5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`).\n127\t\n128\t\n129\tThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\n130\tslice L5) is two tests:\n131\t\n132\t- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\n133\t  processes over real loopback UDP. A JVM publisher with a key file\n134\t  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n135\t  name on all four VMs. Plain Clojure in the test JVM takes the same path\n136\t  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n137\t  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n138\t  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n139\t  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n140\t- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n141\t  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n142\t  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n143\t  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n144\t  REPL.\n145\t\n146\t```sh\n147\t# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\n148\tclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\n149\tclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\n150\tclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n151\t\n152\t# ClojureDart\n153\tclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n154\t\n155\t# Linting\n156\tclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\tThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n160\t[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\n161\tnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\n162\tDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\n163\twith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n164\t`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\n165\texits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\n166\teach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\n167\tscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n168\t<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n169\t(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n170\t`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\n171\tunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\n172\tdifferent namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\n173\tpackage:test names are ns-qualified (`dao.foo-test/bar-test`).\n174\t\n175\t`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\n176\tcompile does not prune it when a source file is deleted or renamed. The\n177\taggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\n178\tstale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\n179\tbefore relying on that to prove a deletion or rename took effect.\n180\t\n181\t## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n182\t\n183\tWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n184\t\n185\tTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n186\t\n187\tWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n188\t1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n189\t2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n190\t3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n191\t\n192\tThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n193\t\n194\t## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n195\t\n196\tA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n197\t\n198\t1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n199\t   ```sh\n200\t   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n201\t   ```\n202\t\n203\t2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n204\t   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n205\t\n206\t3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n207\t   Common patterns:\n208\t   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n209\t   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n210\t   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n211\t\n212\t4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n213\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabb63dd-c047-4e34-a210-01b6c179a82e","uuid":"e0725292-f672-4e7e-a01c-c60a8435de2c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:09:34.011Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6a/docs/agents/build-n-test.md","content":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time repo-wide.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time repo-wide to avoid contention.\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n\n`bb test:sub <subsystem>...` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the tests belonging to\none or more canonical subsystems (defined in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`). Selection\nis by longest namespace prefix matching.\n\n```sh\nbb test:sub <subsystem>...        # All three lanes in parallel (fast form)\nbb test:sub:clj <subsystem>...    # JVM lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>...   # Node lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>...   # Dart lane alone\nbb test:sub:list <subsystem>...   # Show namespaces, builds, Class B seams & dependents; runs nothing\nbb test:sub <subsystem>... --slow # Include slow tests (-i :slow on JVM, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 on Node/Dart)\nbb -cp src/dev -m affected-test   # Run affected-test self-tests directly in Babashka\n```\n\n#### Canonical Subsystems (`src/dev/subsystems.edn`)\n\n- **Layer 0 (Core Data & Transport)**: `dao.stream`, `dao.jing`, `dao.data`, `dao.base`\n- **Layer 1 (Space & UI)**: `dao.space`, `dao.gui`, `dao.postgraphics`\n- **Layer 2 (Execution Engine)**: `yin.vm.ucf`, `yin.vm`\n- **Layer 3 (Languages & Interop)**: `yin.repl`, `yang.python`, `yang.base`\n- **Layer 4 (Applications & Demos)**: `demo`, `world`\n- **Infrastructure**: `dev`, `bench`\n\nPrerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:python-antlr`)\nand lane serialization (`[:clj :cljd]`) are derived purely from text reach of the\nselected namespaces and run automatically when needed.\n\n#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master**: The mandatory landing gate on master after merge, and for any wide change (`bb test`).\n5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`).\n\n\nThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\nslice L5) is two tests:\n\n- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\n  processes over real loopback UDP. A JVM publisher with a key file\n  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n  name on all four VMs. Plain Clojure in the test JVM takes the same path\n  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n  REPL.\n\n```sh\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\nThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\nnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\nDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\nwith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\nexits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\neach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\nscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\nunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\ndifferent namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\npackage:test names are ns-qualified (`dao.foo-test/bar-test`).\n\n`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\ncompile does not prune it when a source file is deleted or renamed. The\naggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\nstale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\nbefore relying on that to prove a deletion or rename took effect.\n\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n","numLines":213,"startLine":1,"totalLines":213}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017ARTM95ZXuXVo7NbXZE7fk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
