{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RLySvCvNyutSAHQbLJ65Rv","type":"tool_result","content":"623\t## 8. Validation on lower\n624\t\n625\tValidation is pure until the last step and checks the whole tree before\n626\tone attachment. The order follows amendment §8 and is binding:\n627\t\n628\t1. **Gate.** Decode the wire map's canonical bytes retaining numeric\n629\t   classes; the tag is present and the outer version is the exact\n630\t   integer 3, else `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` (version found, supported\n631\t   set). Reject duplicate row ids and a `:yin.k/root` that names no\n632\t   `:task` row (`:yin.k/undecodable`). Walk install children from the\n633\t   root in canonical module-name order with an **active recursion-path\n634\t   set** (§3), following only `:install` child crefs; a cref outside the\n635\t   rows, a child already on the active path, or a non-`:task` child\n636\t   stops the gate as `:yin.k/undecodable`; a child reached again off\n637\t   the path is gated once and its result cached. Gate every\n638\t   child's version, then every profile map against the one profile map\n639\t   of §2, then require all versions 3\n640\t   and all profiles equal to the root's. Malformed task structure is\n641\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`; an unsupported version or profile is\n642\t   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`; the two are never conflated.\n643\t2. **Structure, non-recursive.** Every row's kind is tabled with the\n644\t   right arity; every structural slot holds its tabled kind by local\n645\t   inspection; every `V` has one of the three tags; every `D` is in the\n646\t   canonical bytes domain; exactly one row has role `:root`; kind rules\n647\t   of §5.5 hold; the custody slot matches the role, kind and policy\n648\t   table. Nothing in this step follows a reference.\n649\t3. **Graph.** Every cref and every `[:row B]` names a present row of a\n650\t   kind admissible in that position; the structural edge family is\n651\t   acyclic (checked with an active-path walk, bounded by the row count);\n652\t   every row is reachable from the root through structural edges (an\n653\t   unreachable row is `:yin.k/undecodable`); every `[:cursor-cell C]` names a\n654\t   census entry and every census entry is reached **through the task's\n655\t   own roots, the census's declaration edges excluded**, per task and\n656\t   per child; every `:parked-ref` and `parked-id` resolves in the parked\n657\t   table; every `store-of` resolves to a carried module store; every\n658\t   `:install` pending has its entry and every entry's child is a\n659\t   `:child` task. After this step every traversal below is finite and\n660\t   safe.\n661\t4. **Hashes.** Every content row's id equals `(jing/segment-key body)`\n662\t   under the algorithm version 3 mints with, and its address names that\n663\t   algorithm; every code payload hashes to its key `A` and is well formed\n664\t   under the stamp; the requested body address, if one was given, equals\n665\t   the root id. Mismatch is `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` naming the row or\n666\t   code key.\n667\t5. **Canonical form, recursive.** Every literal is in the portable\n668\t   domain; every sorted slot is in the §5 order; every keyed row has\n669\t   unique keys, and every `:set` row unique elements, under canonical\n670\t   bytes and under portable decoded equality; optional absence has its\n671\t   one spelling (nil in the tabled slot); a reference-free collection is\n672\t   spelled `[:lit d]`, never a row; empty collections are literals;\n673\t   metadata obeys §4. A breach is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row\n674\t   and slot. Without this step two different valid encodings could lower\n675\t   to one state, or a `:bindings` row could carry one symbol twice and\n676\t   lose a binding on lower.\n677\t6. **Canonical numbering.** Recompute §6 under the work bound and\n678\t   compare (`:yin.k/undecodable`, kind `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; or the\n679\t   resource refusal of §10.10 if the bound is exceeded).\n680\t7. **Frames.** For each body (the root and every install child), first\n681\t   decode its task context (parked key, live FFI call ids, the root's\n682\t   free environment from `free-env-cref`) and judge it once by\n683\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/task-defect` (continuation §3.2 rule\n684\t   X1: the free environment is a sorted, unique symbol-keyed map with no\n685\t   reserved name); this runs for every body, a `:halted` body with no\n686\t   frames included, since no frame rule establishes X1. Then every\n687\t   `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is\n688\t   decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n689\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n690\t   `:captured`, `:parked`) and that task context; a defect of either\n691\t   function is `:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path\n692\t   (continuation §3.3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6)\n693\t   and before pending validation (step 8).\n694\t8. **Pending and operations.** Reason-specific slot rules; correlation\n695\t   agreement of §5.3 (cursor-cell stream, envelope ids, module names); every\n696\t   op-id below `next-op-seq`, unique across the tree, absent without\n697\t   origin; every install response verified as §5.4 requires.\n698\t9. **Dependency closure.** Compute the census of amendment §6 from the\n699\t   rows (waits, pendings and envelopes, parked records, the initial free\n700\t   environment `free-env`, store, module stores, result, children; the\n701\t   free environment is a root because a value reachable only through it\n702\t   can carry closures, streams and primitives, continuation §7.1) and\n703\t   require the carried `requires` and `code` map to agree with it\n704\t   exactly: a declared segment not reached or a reached segment not\n705\t   declared is `:yin.k/undecodable`, and every reached segment has a\n706\t   non-empty `:yin.k/trees` entry (UCF §7.6.1a). Then\n707\t   evaluate `requires` per UCF §7.6.5: missing segments, primitives,\n708\t   modules, streams, cursor profiles are `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; a body\n709\t   with cursor cells claims `:dao.stream.remote/v1`; module-store coverage is\n710\t   complete for every `store-of` reached.\n711\t10. **Custody.** For an exclusive root, the occurrence, baseline and\n712\t    operation inspector and admission checks of §7.7.8; an authority\n713\t    never adds missing header keys.\n714\t11. **Composition.** Protection, resource, primitive and grant inputs of\n715\t    the receiving composition.\n716\t12. **Restore.** Reconstruct isolated code spaces, fresh values, the\n717\t    isolated store, module-store instances (first link wins), one\n718\t    private resource entry per cursor cell, the parked table, children first\n719\t    (one native task instance **per install entry**, even where two\n720\t    entries share a child row), then waits in order; adopt `max(local,\n721\t    carried)` for the id counter; publish the machine only after every\n722\t    child succeeds; run, poll, mint, append, close or initialize nothing\n723\t    during lower.\n724\t\n725\tDiagnostics use the established families and no new top-level outcome:\n726\t`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, `:yin.k/undecodable` with `:yin.k/path` as\n727\t`[row-id slot-index …]` and a `:yin.k/kind` where one is named above\n728\t(`:reason-mismatch`, `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`), `:yin.k/hash-mismatch`,\n729\t`:yin.k/unsatisfied`, and on the lift side `:yin.k/non-portable` with\n730\tthe two kinds this carrier adds to UCF §7.5.4's set: `:byte-string` and\n731\t`:metadata`.\n732\t\n733\t## 9. Lift, lower, and the laws\n734\t\n735\t**Lift** (reference machine): refuse unless quiescent; number cursor cells (§6);\n736\twalk waits, parked records, the slice, module stores, the initial free\n737\tenvironment (continuation §6.3, §7.1), the result and each install\n738\tchild, emitting rows and the census; refuse by path as UCF\n739\t§7.5.4 and §7.2.1 specify. The nested carrier's value table\n740\t(`:yin.k/values`) has no counterpart, sharing being Merkle; its cursor cell\n741\ttable becomes the census.\n742\t\n743\t**Lower**: §8 in order, then restore.\n744\t\n745\tThe laws, with the domains the Architect's finding 12 requires:\n746\t\n747\t- **Canonical round trip.** For every valid, canonical (§6-numbered)\n748\t  version-3 state `S` under the one profile of §2 **for which `lower(S)`\n749\t  succeeds** (adequate composition, resource and admission inputs; a\n750\t  refusal is not a counterexample), and with no execution between lower\n751\t  and lift, `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id under the **fresh-receiver\n752\t  reconstruction context**: the receiver's id counter is 0 so\n753\t  `max(local, carried)` is the carried value; occurrence, origin and the\n754\t  custody arm are supplied to the lift from the restored task's own\n755\t  record, not minted; cursor-cell bodies and op-ids are carried verbatim; the\n756\t  lift's §6 numbering undoes resource remapping. Outside that context\n757\t  (a receiver with a larger counter, or any step taken) the law does not\n758\t  apply and native equivalence is the claim.\n759\t- **Native observational equivalence.** `lower(lift(m))` need not equal\n760\t  `m` as native state (fresh ids, seals, private keys); under equivalent\n761\t  external inputs it must preserve the next observable step, the wait\n762\t  set and its order, the result, and the effect trace.\n763\t- **Cross-engine.** Running the corpus to each safepoint on an engine\n764\t  that implements canonical semantic-VM execution yields, under\n765\t  controlled composition identities (occurrence, origin, resource\n766\t  descriptors fixed by the harness), the same version-3 row set the\n767\t  reference machine yields.\n768\t\n769\tThe UCF §7.11 harness gains one assertion per law. The Stage D/E corpus,\n770\tre-encoded as version-3 rows, is the oracle for the first law.\n771\t\n772\t## 10. Questions the review answered, and what remains\n773\t\n774\tAnswers 1–6 are the codex Architect's (round 1); where the Architect\n775\tmarked a point as an owner decision it is labelled so.\n776\t\n777\t1. **Occurrence inside the hash.** Kept inside, following the governing\n778\t   rule and binding custody context to the published checkpoint. An\n779\t   occurrence-independent execution-state address is an owner-level\n780\t   protocol decision; if ever pursued it must sit beside, not replace, a\n781\t   fully authenticated checkpoint address, and it does not substitute\n782\t   for the census.\n783\t2. **Packing.** Individual immutable content rows plus a self-contained\n784\t   transport pack. When a pack is addressed it gets its own address and\n785\t   canonical encoding, distinct from the semantic root id; cursor-cell ids\n786\t   remain root-scoped inside it. Same answer as code-as-tuples §2.1\n787\t   should receive; the loader interface is resolved explicitly, not by\n788\t   layout.\n789\t3. **The nested grammar.** Rows are the carrier authority.\n790\t4. **Contract stamp.** The code contract carried is `\"v4\"`, the\n791\t   register-shaped machine's; the carrier version is 3; the two are\n792\t   independent, and neither names a legacy value.\n793\t5. **Reified and parked.** Sharing immutable `:act` rows is acceptable;\n794\t   the two keep distinct outer kinds (§5.1) and distinct lowering. A\n795\t   reified capture has no pending; a parked reference resolves in task\n796\t   context.\n797\t6. **Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an implementation\n798\t   brief claims execution conformance for an engine **outside the three\n799\t   repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and the stack and\n800\t   register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n801\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\n802\t   profile), and not drafted here: admitted values, numeric behaviour,\n803\t   key equality, metadata, resource and profile requirements, refusal\n804\t   sets, and safepoint reconstruction obligations. Slot losslessness\n805\t   alone does not establish execution parity; version 3 carries the\n806\t   canonical frame; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through\n807\t   its layout (continuation §4), which is heterogeneous reconstruction,\n808\t   not translation between native formats; foreign-engine *value*\n809\t   profiles for engines outside this repository remain a separate\n810\t   document.\n811\t\n812\tAnswers 7–9 are the Architect's (round 2) and are adopted (7 and 8 are\n813\tdeleted 2026-10-11: there are no other profile tables and no legacy\n814\treader):\n815\t\n816\t9. **Skeleton placeholder.** Safe only if the full value-union tag is\n817\t   retained in the skeleton, which §6 now requires (`[:cursor-cell <class>]`,\n818\t   never a bare class); and a placeholder does not canonicalize alias\n819\t   topology, which is why §6 is now defined as the output of a\n820\t   renaming-invariant refinement-and-search procedure.\n821\t\n822\t10. **Receiver work bound** (Architect, round 3; adopted as a\n823\t    requirement, with the limits left to implementation and\n824\t    composition). Before an implementation brief, the receiver must have\n825\t    a bound on decoded bytes, rows, cursor cells, traversal depth, refinement\n826\t    work and search nodes for §6, with elapsed time as an optional\n827\t    operational limit on top. Exceeding a local budget produces a\n828\t    structured resource or capability refusal before any attachment, in\n829\t    the qualified-unsupported family `datom.world.md` already provides;\n830\t    it never labels a valid state `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, never falls\n831\t    back to encounter order, and never accepts an unfinished check. The\n832\t    exact limits and their refusal mapping are implementation and\n833\t    composition decisions and must not alter canonical bytes.\n834\t\n835\t**Proposals, not consequences.** The following are design choices this\n836\tdocument makes; they follow neither uniquely from the owner's three\n837\trulings nor from the six invariants, and an implementation brief must\n838\tname them as choices being accepted: a new body version (3) rather than\n839\tanother carrier identification; the canonical representative of §6 as\n840\tdefined by its procedure; the wire unit and pack framing of §3; the\n841\texplicit fork-policy spelling of §5.5; one engine-less profile\n842\t(continuation §2.1); the explicit root `free-env` (continuation §6.3);\n843\tthe byte-string and metadata restrictions of §4; binding the row digest to\n844\tthe carrier version rather than to a named algorithm (§3; the owner\n845\truled 2026-10-10 that rows use the same digest as code addresses, which\n846\tis Jing's default, rather than a separate SHA-256 pin); and positional\n847\trows over EAV (§1). Preserving the complete FFI\n848\tenvelope (§5.3) is *not* on this list: it is the inherited behaviour,\n849\tand narrowing it would have been the new protocol decision.\n850\t\n851\tStill open after this revision: none beyond the work-bound limits\n852\t(§10.10).\n853\t\n854\t## 11. What this does not change\n855\t\n856\tCode identity (A), safepoints,\n857\tpending-wait semantics and the r5 required keys, install-child rules,\n858\tthe dependency closure and satisfaction check, the isolated store, the\n859\tprivate resource table, module-store instancing, scheduler state, the\n860\tcustody header and admission rules, fencing and operation ids, the\n861\toutcome families, and the existing refusal kinds (two lift kinds and two\n862\t`:yin.k/undecodable` kinds are added, §8). The carrier is a new body\n863\tversion for the same facts. The\n864\tArchitect's round-1 statement is the acceptance bar: tuple transport\n865\tviolates none of the six invariants once polymorphic references and\n866\tcontext edges are specified and validated, and §4, §3 and §8 are where\n867\tthey are."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabb63dd-c047-4e34-a210-01b6c179a82e","uuid":"804ee456-9f8b-416a-8c99-d9e5cba049fe","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:35:33.001Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6a/collab/1792250000000-carrier.master.md","content":"## 8. Validation on lower\n\nValidation is pure until the last step and checks the whole tree before\none attachment. The order follows amendment §8 and is binding:\n\n1. **Gate.** Decode the wire map's canonical bytes retaining numeric\n   classes; the tag is present and the outer version is the exact\n   integer 3, else `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` (version found, supported\n   set). Reject duplicate row ids and a `:yin.k/root` that names no\n   `:task` row (`:yin.k/undecodable`). Walk install children from the\n   root in canonical module-name order with an **active recursion-path\n   set** (§3), following only `:install` child crefs; a cref outside the\n   rows, a child already on the active path, or a non-`:task` child\n   stops the gate as `:yin.k/undecodable`; a child reached again off\n   the path is gated once and its result cached. Gate every\n   child's version, then every profile map against the one profile map\n   of §2, then require all versions 3\n   and all profiles equal to the root's. Malformed task structure is\n   `:yin.k/undecodable`; an unsupported version or profile is\n   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`; the two are never conflated.\n2. **Structure, non-recursive.** Every row's kind is tabled with the\n   right arity; every structural slot holds its tabled kind by local\n   inspection; every `V` has one of the three tags; every `D` is in the\n   canonical bytes domain; exactly one row has role `:root`; kind rules\n   of §5.5 hold; the custody slot matches the role, kind and policy\n   table. Nothing in this step follows a reference.\n3. **Graph.** Every cref and every `[:row B]` names a present row of a\n   kind admissible in that position; the structural edge family is\n   acyclic (checked with an active-path walk, bounded by the row count);\n   every row is reachable from the root through structural edges (an\n   unreachable row is `:yin.k/undecodable`); every `[:cursor-cell C]` names a\n   census entry and every census entry is reached **through the task's\n   own roots, the census's declaration edges excluded**, per task and\n   per child; every `:parked-ref` and `parked-id` resolves in the parked\n   table; every `store-of` resolves to a carried module store; every\n   `:install` pending has its entry and every entry's child is a\n   `:child` task. After this step every traversal below is finite and\n   safe.\n4. **Hashes.** Every content row's id equals `(jing/segment-key body)`\n   under the algorithm version 3 mints with, and its address names that\n   algorithm; every code payload hashes to its key `A` and is well formed\n   under the stamp; the requested body address, if one was given, equals\n   the root id. Mismatch is `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` naming the row or\n   code key.\n5. **Canonical form, recursive.** Every literal is in the portable\n   domain; every sorted slot is in the §5 order; every keyed row has\n   unique keys, and every `:set` row unique elements, under canonical\n   bytes and under portable decoded equality; optional absence has its\n   one spelling (nil in the tabled slot); a reference-free collection is\n   spelled `[:lit d]`, never a row; empty collections are literals;\n   metadata obeys §4. A breach is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row\n   and slot. Without this step two different valid encodings could lower\n   to one state, or a `:bindings` row could carry one symbol twice and\n   lose a binding on lower.\n6. **Canonical numbering.** Recompute §6 under the work bound and\n   compare (`:yin.k/undecodable`, kind `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; or the\n   resource refusal of §10.10 if the bound is exceeded).\n7. **Frames.** For each body (the root and every install child), first\n   decode its task context (parked key, live FFI call ids, the root's\n   free environment from `free-env-cref`) and judge it once by\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/task-defect` (continuation §3.2 rule\n   X1: the free environment is a sorted, unique symbol-keyed map with no\n   reserved name); this runs for every body, a `:halted` body with no\n   frames included, since no frame rule establishes X1. Then every\n   `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and parked-table state is\n   decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n   `:captured`, `:parked`) and that task context; a defect of either\n   function is `:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path\n   (continuation §3.3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6)\n   and before pending validation (step 8).\n8. **Pending and operations.** Reason-specific slot rules; correlation\n   agreement of §5.3 (cursor-cell stream, envelope ids, module names); every\n   op-id below `next-op-seq`, unique across the tree, absent without\n   origin; every install response verified as §5.4 requires.\n9. **Dependency closure.** Compute the census of amendment §6 from the\n   rows (waits, pendings and envelopes, parked records, the initial free\n   environment `free-env`, store, module stores, result, children; the\n   free environment is a root because a value reachable only through it\n   can carry closures, streams and primitives, continuation §7.1) and\n   require the carried `requires` and `code` map to agree with it\n   exactly: a declared segment not reached or a reached segment not\n   declared is `:yin.k/undecodable`, and every reached segment has a\n   non-empty `:yin.k/trees` entry (UCF §7.6.1a). Then\n   evaluate `requires` per UCF §7.6.5: missing segments, primitives,\n   modules, streams, cursor profiles are `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; a body\n   with cursor cells claims `:dao.stream.remote/v1`; module-store coverage is\n   complete for every `store-of` reached.\n10. **Custody.** For an exclusive root, the occurrence, baseline and\n    operation inspector and admission checks of §7.7.8; an authority\n    never adds missing header keys.\n11. **Composition.** Protection, resource, primitive and grant inputs of\n    the receiving composition.\n12. **Restore.** Reconstruct isolated code spaces, fresh values, the\n    isolated store, module-store instances (first link wins), one\n    private resource entry per cursor cell, the parked table, children first\n    (one native task instance **per install entry**, even where two\n    entries share a child row), then waits in order; adopt `max(local,\n    carried)` for the id counter; publish the machine only after every\n    child succeeds; run, poll, mint, append, close or initialize nothing\n    during lower.\n\nDiagnostics use the established families and no new top-level outcome:\n`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, `:yin.k/undecodable` with `:yin.k/path` as\n`[row-id slot-index …]` and a `:yin.k/kind` where one is named above\n(`:reason-mismatch`, `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`), `:yin.k/hash-mismatch`,\n`:yin.k/unsatisfied`, and on the lift side `:yin.k/non-portable` with\nthe two kinds this carrier adds to UCF §7.5.4's set: `:byte-string` and\n`:metadata`.\n\n## 9. Lift, lower, and the laws\n\n**Lift** (reference machine): refuse unless quiescent; number cursor cells (§6);\nwalk waits, parked records, the slice, module stores, the initial free\nenvironment (continuation §6.3, §7.1), the result and each install\nchild, emitting rows and the census; refuse by path as UCF\n§7.5.4 and §7.2.1 specify. The nested carrier's value table\n(`:yin.k/values`) has no counterpart, sharing being Merkle; its cursor cell\ntable becomes the census.\n\n**Lower**: §8 in order, then restore.\n\nThe laws, with the domains the Architect's finding 12 requires:\n\n- **Canonical round trip.** For every valid, canonical (§6-numbered)\n  version-3 state `S` under the one profile of §2 **for which `lower(S)`\n  succeeds** (adequate composition, resource and admission inputs; a\n  refusal is not a counterexample), and with no execution between lower\n  and lift, `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id under the **fresh-receiver\n  reconstruction context**: the receiver's id counter is 0 so\n  `max(local, carried)` is the carried value; occurrence, origin and the\n  custody arm are supplied to the lift from the restored task's own\n  record, not minted; cursor-cell bodies and op-ids are carried verbatim; the\n  lift's §6 numbering undoes resource remapping. Outside that context\n  (a receiver with a larger counter, or any step taken) the law does not\n  apply and native equivalence is the claim.\n- **Native observational equivalence.** `lower(lift(m))` need not equal\n  `m` as native state (fresh ids, seals, private keys); under equivalent\n  external inputs it must preserve the next observable step, the wait\n  set and its order, the result, and the effect trace.\n- **Cross-engine.** Running the corpus to each safepoint on an engine\n  that implements canonical semantic-VM execution yields, under\n  controlled composition identities (occurrence, origin, resource\n  descriptors fixed by the harness), the same version-3 row set the\n  reference machine yields.\n\nThe UCF §7.11 harness gains one assertion per law. The Stage D/E corpus,\nre-encoded as version-3 rows, is the oracle for the first law.\n\n## 10. Questions the review answered, and what remains\n\nAnswers 1–6 are the codex Architect's (round 1); where the Architect\nmarked a point as an owner decision it is labelled so.\n\n1. **Occurrence inside the hash.** Kept inside, following the governing\n   rule and binding custody context to the published checkpoint. An\n   occurrence-independent execution-state address is an owner-level\n   protocol decision; if ever pursued it must sit beside, not replace, a\n   fully authenticated checkpoint address, and it does not substitute\n   for the census.\n2. **Packing.** Individual immutable content rows plus a self-contained\n   transport pack. When a pack is addressed it gets its own address and\n   canonical encoding, distinct from the semantic root id; cursor-cell ids\n   remain root-scoped inside it. Same answer as code-as-tuples §2.1\n   should receive; the loader interface is resolved explicitly, not by\n   layout.\n3. **The nested grammar.** Rows are the carrier authority.\n4. **Contract stamp.** The code contract carried is `\"v4\"`, the\n   register-shaped machine's; the carrier version is 3; the two are\n   independent, and neither names a legacy value.\n5. **Reified and parked.** Sharing immutable `:act` rows is acceptable;\n   the two keep distinct outer kinds (§5.1) and distinct lowering. A\n   reified capture has no pending; a parked reference resolves in task\n   context.\n6. **Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an implementation\n   brief claims execution conformance for an engine **outside the three\n   repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and the stack and\n   register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n   `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\n   profile), and not drafted here: admitted values, numeric behaviour,\n   key equality, metadata, resource and profile requirements, refusal\n   sets, and safepoint reconstruction obligations. Slot losslessness\n   alone does not establish execution parity; version 3 carries the\n   canonical frame; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through\n   its layout (continuation §4), which is heterogeneous reconstruction,\n   not translation between native formats; foreign-engine *value*\n   profiles for engines outside this repository remain a separate\n   document.\n\nAnswers 7–9 are the Architect's (round 2) and are adopted (7 and 8 are\ndeleted 2026-10-11: there are no other profile tables and no legacy\nreader):\n\n9. **Skeleton placeholder.** Safe only if the full value-union tag is\n   retained in the skeleton, which §6 now requires (`[:cursor-cell <class>]`,\n   never a bare class); and a placeholder does not canonicalize alias\n   topology, which is why §6 is now defined as the output of a\n   renaming-invariant refinement-and-search procedure.\n\n10. **Receiver work bound** (Architect, round 3; adopted as a\n    requirement, with the limits left to implementation and\n    composition). Before an implementation brief, the receiver must have\n    a bound on decoded bytes, rows, cursor cells, traversal depth, refinement\n    work and search nodes for §6, with elapsed time as an optional\n    operational limit on top. Exceeding a local budget produces a\n    structured resource or capability refusal before any attachment, in\n    the qualified-unsupported family `datom.world.md` already provides;\n    it never labels a valid state `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, never falls\n    back to encounter order, and never accepts an unfinished check. The\n    exact limits and their refusal mapping are implementation and\n    composition decisions and must not alter canonical bytes.\n\n**Proposals, not consequences.** The following are design choices this\ndocument makes; they follow neither uniquely from the owner's three\nrulings nor from the six invariants, and an implementation brief must\nname them as choices being accepted: a new body version (3) rather than\nanother carrier identification; the canonical representative of §6 as\ndefined by its procedure; the wire unit and pack framing of §3; the\nexplicit fork-policy spelling of §5.5; one engine-less profile\n(continuation §2.1); the explicit root `free-env` (continuation §6.3);\nthe byte-string and metadata restrictions of §4; binding the row digest to\nthe carrier version rather than to a named algorithm (§3; the owner\nruled 2026-10-10 that rows use the same digest as code addresses, which\nis Jing's default, rather than a separate SHA-256 pin); and positional\nrows over EAV (§1). Preserving the complete FFI\nenvelope (§5.3) is *not* on this list: it is the inherited behaviour,\nand narrowing it would have been the new protocol decision.\n\nStill open after this revision: none beyond the work-bound limits\n(§10.10).\n\n## 11. What this does not change\n\nCode identity (A), safepoints,\npending-wait semantics and the r5 required keys, install-child rules,\nthe dependency closure and satisfaction check, the isolated store, the\nprivate resource table, module-store instancing, scheduler state, the\ncustody header and admission rules, fencing and operation ids, the\noutcome families, and the existing refusal kinds (two lift kinds and two\n`:yin.k/undecodable` kinds are added, §8). The carrier is a new body\nversion for the same facts. The\nArchitect's round-1 statement is the acceptance bar: tuple transport\nviolates none of the six invariants once polymorphic references and\ncontext edges are specified and validated, and §4, §3 and §8 are where\nthey are.","numLines":245,"startLine":623,"totalLines":868}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RLySvCvNyutSAHQbLJ65Rv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
