{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Shx4GvJ8PNwURncxwzYETF","type":"tool_result","content":"1072\t## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n1073\t\n1074\tVerification follows `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: G0 per iteration on\n1075\tthe JVM, G1 `bb test:sub yin.vm` on three hosts, G2 `bb test:changed`,\n1076\tG3 on master.\n1077\t\n1078\t### 8.1 Slice 6a: the frame validator and the row codec (independent)\n1079\t\n1080\t**Files to create.**\n1081\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` (§3): `defect`, public.\n1082\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (§2): the row table as data,\n1083\t  `frame->rows`, `rows->frame`, row ids (Jing default), the census and\n1084\t  numbering per the draft §6, `canonical-under` (§5.5, test-only but\n1085\t  placed here so three test namespaces share it). **Not** `lift-task`/\n1086\t  `lower-task`: full task transport is 6b.\n1087\t- `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc`,\n1088\t  `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc`.\n1089\t\n1090\t**Depends on:** phase 3, 4a (landed), 4b stage 1 (branch) for live\n1091\tframes to validate. Touches nothing of 4b or 5; needs no scanner.\n1092\t\n1093\t**Acceptance (6a).**\n1094\t\n1095\t1. `frame-test/contract-is-pure`: `frame/defect` takes `[frame code\n1096\t   context task]`, `task` being plain data; the namespace's `ns` form\n1097\t   requires no kernel and no `yin.vm.engine` (a string check over the\n1098\t   source on the JVM lane, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`).\n1099\t2. `frame-test/every-reference-frame-validates`: for every 4b-stage-1\n1100\t   row of §5.2 (1, 2, 5, 6, 13-16, 18, 19, 21, 22) over the four segments,\n1101\t   plus row 20 as one separate, unwrapped run (its empty `K` needs no wrapper\n1102\t   frames; §8.2 6b makes the same exception), every\n1103\t   `act`, `tail`, return frame, parked record and reified value the\n1104\t   register evaluator mints passes `defect` in its context with the\n1105\t   task context decoded from the machine's own tables.\n1106\t3. `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper`: for each rule S1-S4, C1-C3,\n1107\t   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\n1108\t   valid one, refused with that rule's kind and a path naming the slot\n1109\t   (**twenty-four rules**: 4+3+6+1+3+2+1+4, the twenty-three of the\n1110\t   round-1 text plus X1; **twenty-five rows**, since C2 contributes two,\n1111\t   a float `pc` for `:pc-kind` and an out-of-range one for `:pc-bounds`;\n1112\t   X1's row goes through `frame/task-defect`); plus\n1113\t   `first-defect-is-structural`: a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a\n1114\t   bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n1115\t4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n1116\t   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n1117\t   removed is `:window-missing`.\n1118\t5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n1119\t   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n1120\t   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n1121\t   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n1122\t6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame (initial free\n1123\t   environment `{x 99 y 7}`) with `task :free-env {x 99 y 7}` validates;\n1124\t   with the free environment `{x 99 y 8}` or `{x 99}` it is\n1125\t   `:free-env-mismatch` (`y` is unshadowed); with the lexical `x` removed\n1126\t   from `E` it is `:free-env-mismatch` (presence); changing the lexical\n1127\t   `x` in `E` from `1` to `98` **does not** trip E2 (it is off the\n1128\t   comparison), and the test asserts that too; a `free-env` row with the\n1129\t   key `yin/def` is `:reserved-name` (X1).\n1130\t7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n1131\t   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n1132\t8. `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`: every content row's id equals\n1133\t   `(jing/segment-key body)` and names Jing's default algorithm; no\n1134\t   `sha256` appears in any id.\n1135\t9. `rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique`: an out-of-order or duplicated\n1136\t   `:window` row is `:yin.k/undecodable` at canonical form (step 5).\n1137\t10. `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`: §5.5's\n1138\t    transformation gives equal root ids for two emissions of one abstract\n1139\t    task under permuted cursor-cell numbering and distinct stream identities,\n1140\t    with the fixture's correspondence map; **and the unordered-container\n1141\t    permutation**: a store value that is a set of two stream references\n1142\t    and a map keyed by two cursor references, emitted twice with the two\n1143\t    streams' identities swapped (and the correspondence map swapped\n1144\t    accordingly), gives equal root ids; a marker absent from the map is\n1145\t    a test failure.\n1146\t11. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log\n1147\t    shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and\n1148\t    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n1149\t\n1150\t### 8.2 Slice 6b: full task transport and the harness on the reference lane\n1151\t\n1152\t**Files to change.** `rows.cljc`: `lift-task`, `lower-task` (§7), the\n1153\tpending rows' lift and lower, install children. **Files to create.**\n1154\t`test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\n1155\t`:semantic-register` lane). The old harness file is not edited.\n1156\t\n1157\t**Depends on:** the explicit `:free-env` lift argument supplied by the\n1158\tharness (§6.3; the 4b retention seam is a named follow-up for the 4b\n1159\ttrack, not a 6b prerequisite); 4b stage 2 (FFI retained→sent restoration, link\n1160\trequest/response/install preservation, install children, the\n1161\tevaluator's `IModuleKernel` linking methods: `link-format`,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabb63dd-c047-4e34-a210-01b6c179a82e","uuid":"5f65fd26-a18c-4162-9551-03fdc5686b3d","timestamp":