{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxMgXJ9p32ncwcciWBjY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Discovery-order numbering is in `rows.cljc` and the tests are rewritten. Kondo is clean and the JVM lanes are green; Node and Dart were not run, per the brief. Nothing is committed. Two things didn't go to plan: **I couldn't merge master**, and **the doc amendments are a patch** rather than edits in the worktree.\n\n**Merge blocked.** `git merge master` needed an approval this session couldn't grant, so the branch is unmerged. Master changes nothing in `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/` or `rows_test`, so the code should merge cleanly. The docs are the problem: master renamed \"cell\" to \"cursor cell\" throughout the carrier and continuation docs, and the branch has the old text. So I applied A1–A9 to master's text and wrote it as `collab/1792250000000-docs-amendments-against-master.patch`, with the full amended copies beside it. To land it:\n1. Merge master.\n2. `git apply` the patch.\n3. Copy `collab/numbering-ref/note.md` to `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md`. The amendments link to it by that name and it isn't on master yet. Its status line still says \"not yet implemented\".\n\n**Results (JVM):**\n- Before any change: rows-test plus frame-test, 31 tests, 554 assertions, all passing.\n- After: rows-test with the slow test, 30 tests and 461 assertions; all `yin.vm.ucf.*` plus frame-test (fast tier), 688 tests and 12,299 assertions. 0 failures in both.\n- The generator found no root mismatches and no decode failures over 3,300 slow states and 410 quick ones.\n- **Pins:** every pin and numbering in the note reproduced on the first run, none re-pinned: 6a's 14 roots, including `fab223…`, `c4a7c7…`, `2d9873a8…`, `0193312…` and `387f294a…`, plus the new ones (`5376f133…`, `d84480d4…`, `726a9fbb…`, `e67405ec…` and the two frame fixtures). All the refusal paths and cells matched too. `55ff168e…` is gone: the loop plus 2-cycle now refuses at `[15]` with cells `[:a :b]`.\n- **Size:** rows.cljc is +536/−178, against the note's estimate of about +280/−135. The procedure itself is about 420 non-blank lines, close to the probe's 405. The rest is code that moved, re-indentation and docstrings.\n\n**Mutation checks:**\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Drop the occurrence count | Caught by the pins |\n| Drop the first-occurrence index | Caught: the balanced-alias witness gives two different roots |\n| Reverse a passing tie group's order | Survives, as it should: the proof says this order can't change the rows |\n| Enter a failing tie group in host order | Caught |\n| Skip the tie test's confinement check | Caught |\n| Skip the representation charge | Caught |\n| Skip the depth scan's charge | Caught |\n| Validate frames before numbering | Caught |\n\nI read \"make a tie order depend on host enumeration\" two ways; only the failing-group version is a real defect. That one and the skipped confinement check slip past the note's three generators, so I added the reviewer's tie-heavy incidence families to the search; with those, the generator catches both on its own.\n\n**Deviations from the note** (full list in the report):\n- **`emit-numbered`** takes an optional function for numbering install children. Without it the test carrier for an install child holding the 2-cycle can't be built.\n- **`canonical-numbering`** takes an optional counter atom, so tests can check the work counter at 2001 and the estimator step count.\n- **Child budgets:** install children are numbered under the caller's budget; 6a used the default.\n- **Empty census** still returns `{}` before the depth scan, which is 6a's contract.\n- **`schema-and-literal-canonicality`** (a kept test) now builds two carriers with `emit-numbered`, because the lift itself refuses those states: one is the totality defect, the other a tie.\n- **Carrier §6:** I dropped the note's `rows.cljc` line references and appendix figures from the spec text, since they would go stale.\n\n**For the Node and Dart runs:**\n- `test/cljd-out` holds stale generated tests; clear it before trusting a plain `cljd test`.\n- The large-literal test (1.9 s on the JVM) and the quick generator (about 1.5 s) may go over 5 s on those hosts. If so, tag them `^:slow`.\n\nThe report is `collab/1792250000000-engineer-6a-discovery-numbering.report.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9243,"cache_read_input_tokens":290852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9243},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabb63dd-c047-4e34-a210-01b6c179a82e","uuid":"f84f3881-0cd6-4511-9ef3-575281f43ee9","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:39:33.420Z","request_id":"req_011CfxMgWXWgP6mXKUyS8SVR"}
