fab223…`, `c4a7c7…`, `2d9873a8…`, `0193312…` and `387f294a…`, plus the new ones (`5376f133…`, `d84480d4…`, `726a9fbb…`, `e67405ec…` and the two frame fixtures). All the refusal paths and cells matched too. `55ff168e…` is gone: the loop plus 2-cycle now refuses at `[15]` with cells `[:a :b]`.\n- **Size:** rows.cljc is +536/−178, against the note's estimate of about +280/−135. The procedure itself is about 420 non-blank lines, close to the probe's 405. The rest is code that moved, re-indentation and docstrings.\n\n**Mutation checks:**\n\n| Mutant | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Drop the occurrence count | Caught by the pins |\n| Drop the first-occurrence index | Caught: the balanced-alias witness gives two different roots |\n| Reverse a passing tie group's order | Survives, as it should: the proof says this order can't change the rows |\n| Enter a failing tie group in host order | Caught |\n| Skip the tie test's confinement check | Caught |\n| Skip the representation charge | Caught |\n| Skip the depth scan's charge | Caught |\n| Validate frames before numbering | Caught |\n\nI read \"make a tie order depend on host enumeration\" two ways; only the failing-group version is a real defect. That one and the skipped confinement check slip past the note's three generators, so I added the reviewer's tie-heavy incidence families to the search; with those, the generator catches both on its own.\n\n**Deviations from the note** (full list in the report):\n- **`emit-numbered`** takes an optional function for numbering install children. Without it the test carrier for an install child holding the 2-cycle can't be built.\n- **`canonical-numbering`** takes an optional counter atom, so tests can check the work counter at 2001 and the estimator step count.\n- **Child budgets:** install children are numbered under the caller's budget; 6a used the default.\n- **Empty census** still returns `{}` before the depth scan, which is 6a's contract.\n- **`schema-and-literal-canonicality`** (a kept test) now builds two carriers with `emit-numbered`, because the lift itself refuses those states: one is the totality defect, the other a tie.\n- **Carrier §6:** I dropped the note's `rows.cljc` line references and appendix figures from the spec text, since they would go stale.\n\n**For the Node and Dart runs:**\n- `test/cljd-out` holds stale generated tests; clear it before trusting a plain `cljd test`.\n- The large-literal test (1.9 s on the JVM) and the quick generator (about 1.5 s) may go over 5 s on those hosts. If so, tag them `^:slow`.\n\nThe report is `collab/1792250000000-engineer-6a-discovery-numbering.report.md`.","ttft_ms":1575,"type":"result","duration_ms":1806217,"uuid":"17bc1ccb-f9e8-422e-be4b-127ccd7c84eb","ttft_stream_ms":1452,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1452,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
